description:
**Job Duties / Responsibilities:**


* Familiar with PLC (Step7/RSLogix5000,etc.) / DCS technologies;
* Familiar with HMI technologies (IFix / FactoryTalkViewSE / WinCC);
* Familiar with ABB S\\+ Operation and/or S\\+ Engineer will be an advantage;
* Familiar with AutoCAD and system drawings;
* Response for control engineering projects site installation, commissioning and assist project hand over;
* Take lead in any ad\\-hoc tasks when necessary.

**Requirement:**


* Degree holder in Industrial Automation/ Electrical / Computer Science Engineering or related disciplines is preferable;
* High diplomas with related solid work experience are also welcome
* 2 years of solid work experience in PLC/DCS/HMI (Control, Automation) is preferable;
* Good communication in Cantonese, Mandarin, and English;
* Work experience in the power plant or DSD would be an advantage;
* Strong sense of responsibility, self\\-motivated, good teamwork;

**Working Details:**  




* Working place – Tuen Mun
* 5 Days work

**Apply****：**



For interested applicants, please send your full CV to our Human Resources Department (cal\\_hr@controlautomation.com.hk ) for application.




*The information provided will be treated in strict confidence and used only for consideration of the application for relevant/similar post(s). All personal data of unsuccessful applicants will be destroyed within 6 months.*

**Company Introduction**
Founded in 1862, The Hong Kong and China Gas Company Limited (Towngas) was Hong Kong's first public utility. Today, we are one of the largest energy suppliers in Hong Kong, operating with world\\-class corporate management and leading\\-edge business practices. For the past years, Towngas has been growing with Hong Kong, evolving from the simple gas company supplying fuel for street lamps to our current leading position in the energy industry in the greater China region.
**The Job**
* Deliver project management functions for various renovation \\& building facilities upgrade projects;


* Develop and implement control workflow in executing project management;


* Liaise and coordinate with consultants, contractors and users on project management;


* Administer the contractors’ working safety standard manual and assess contractors’ performance scores;


* Assist on contract administration and project management, from project inception to handover to users;


* Prepare design / technical specifications and tender documents for fitting\\-out works; alteration and addition works, repair and maintenance works;


* Design and implement improvements on existing technical systems and office renovation;


* Perform ad hoc duties assigned by supervisor

**The Person**
* Degree or above in Building Services Engineering, Building Studies, Project Management, or equivalent;


* Minimum of 8 years’ relevant experience of which 5 years should be in management position;


* Membership in HKIE (The Hong Kong Institution of Engineers) or equivalent is preferred;


* Holder of Registered Electrical Worker (License A or B) will be added advantage;


* Holder of a valid driving license is an added advantage;


* Work independently and self\\-motivated;


* Willing to develop multi\\-skills in managing building renovation and related projects;


* Proficient in interior design software, CAD, Microsoft Office and Chinese word processing;


* Proficient in spoken and written English and Chinese; fluent Putonghua is an added advantage;


* Occasional travel to the PRC is required

**Application Method**
Application with full details stating current and expected salary to: recruit@towngas.com or click “Apply Now” to submit online application.
Deadline for application: 13 December 2025
Please quote the reference number (PMD/APM/TG01/25\\) in your application.
(All personal data provided will be treated in strict confidence and used for recruitment purposes only.)
